# Security & Authentication
- Authentication checks must be the absolute first line of code in any protected Route Handler or Server Action.
- Never log sensitive user data, passwords, API keys, or full request payloads to the console.
- Sanitize any user-generated content that will be rendered using `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
- Keep secrets and server-only service configuration in environment variables without the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix. Never expose them to Client Components, browser bundles, rendered props, public responses, or logs.
- Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_` only for values explicitly designed to be public. Do not treat a public Supabase URL or publishable key as authorization; enforce Row Level Security and server-side authorization.
- Validate environment variables in a central Zod schema, and mark modules that read server-only configuration with `import "server-only"`.
- Route browser data access through narrowly scoped, feature-specific Route Handlers or Server Actions that authenticate, authorize, and validate inputs. Do not build a generic database proxy or send privileged keys to the browser.